{{> Top}}<section id="latest" class="results" aria-live="polite">
{{#racer}}<p class="racer"><span class="news">{{ text }}</span><span class="items"><span class="row">{{#items}}<span class="item">{{ . }}</span>{{/items}}</span></span></p>
{{/racer}}{{?ready}}<p class="run-meta"><span>Race <b>{{ id }}</b></span> <span>{{ started }}</span>{{?timed}} <span>{{ took }}</span>{{/timed}}</p>
<p class="run-meta">{{#commits}}<span>{{ name }} <a href="{{ url }}">{{ short }}</a></span> {{/commits}}</p>
<ul class="legend" aria-label="Competitors">{{#competitors}}<li><span class="swatch s-{{ . }}"></span><a href="/competitors">{{ . }}</a></li>{{/competitors}}<li><span class="swatch hollow-bar"></span>server not saturated</li></ul>
{{> RaceClasses}}{{/ready}}{{^ready}}<p class="pending">No race yet: the first nightly has not run.</p>{{/ready}}
</section>
<article class="prose">
<h2>How it runs</h2>
<ul>
<li>A race runs each night when fourneau, roux or this repository has a new commit. Each result names the commits it raced.</li>
<li>Each server class gets fresh DigitalOcean droplets: the server on one, the load generator (<a href="https://github.com/hatoo/oha">oha</a>) on a bigger one, over the private network.</li>
<li>Workloads raced flat out, each a part of a server&rsquo;s job, in rounds of random order; the median counts, of throughput and of each latency percentile.</li>
<li>And one with a database: RealWorld&rsquo;s Conduit API on SQLite, reads and writes at once, offered at the same rising rates to every server.</li>
<li>Each over plain HTTP/1.1, as behind a proxy; the realistic ones again over HTTP/2 and TLS, as browsers reach a server with no proxy (the tabs beside the sizes).</li>
</ul>
<p>Details: <a href="/workloads">Workloads</a>, <a href="/method">Method</a>. To make a server faster or add one: <a href="/contribute">Contribute</a>.</p>
</article>
{{> Bottom}}
